Build-system integration for the DAOS plugin, against ai-dynamo/nixl main.

Three edits; the plugin sources themselves live in plugin/ and are copied to
src/plugins/daos/. Kept as a patch rather than a fork because it is small and
because upstream may take the plugin, at which point this file disappears.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ all_plugins
-all_plugins = ['UCX', 'LIBFABRIC', 'POSIX', 'OBJ', ...
+all_plugins = ['UCX', 'LIBFABRIC', 'POSIX', 'DAOS', 'OBJ', ...

@@ before "# Check for POSIX aio"
+# DAOS client library. Looked up here rather than in the plugin so the gate in
+# src/plugins/meson.build can skip the subdir when it is absent.
+daos_dep = meson.get_compiler('cpp').find_library('daos', required: false)
+
 # Check for POSIX aio

--- a/src/plugins/meson.build
+++ b/src/plugins/meson.build
@@ before the OBJ block
+if enabled_plugins.get('DAOS')
+    subdir('daos')
+endif
+
 if enabled_plugins.get('OBJ')

Note: `cc` is not yet defined at that point in the root meson.build -- it is
introduced later, in src/plugins/meson.build -- so the lookup must use
meson.get_compiler('cpp') directly.
